  "text": "Beneath the streetlamps’ ghostly gleam,\nHe walked the city’s hollow dream.\nEach footfall rang on stone and street,\nWhere shadows and the silent meet.\n\nLike phantoms passed the hurried crowd,\nWith eyes cast down, in solitude.\nNo glance was cast, no word was said,\nBy those who walked, but never led.\n\nAmidst the urban, vast expanse,\nHe felt the weight of empty chance.\nA profound solitude took hold,\nA story left forever untold.\n\nThe animal known for its long neck is the giraffe."
